[2026-05-31T15:57:16.087454] [INFO] Node Chief Product Officer - Event EventType.TOOL_CALL - Tool call save_file for node Chief Product Officer Details: {'tool_result': None, 'tool_name': 'save_file', 'success': None, 'result_size': 0, 'arguments': {'path': 'lice/manual.md', 'content': "# Lice Project User Manual\n\n## Introduction\nThe **Lice** project is a tool designed to quickly generate license files for software projects. It supports a wide range of commonly used open-source licenses, aiming to save time for developers and ensure that software licensing is handled correctly and efficiently.\n\n## Main Functions\n- **License Generation**: Generate license files for various open-source licenses.\n- **Support for Multiple Licenses**: Choose from a wide range of commonly used licenses.\n- **Time-Saving**: Efficiently create license files without manual intervention.\n\n## Environment Setup\nTo get started with the Lice project, you'll need to set up the Python environment and install the necessary dependencies. Follow these steps:\n\n### Step 1: Install Python\nEnsure you have Python installed on your machine. You can download it from [python.org](https://www.python.org/downloads/).\n\n### Step 2: Create a Virtual Environment\nIt is recommended to create a virtual environment to manage project dependencies. Run the following command in your terminal:\n\n```bash\npython -m venv venv\n```\n\n### Step 3: Activate the Virtual Environment\nActivate the virtual environment using the following command:\n- On Windows:\n    ```bash\n    venv\\Scripts\\activate\n    ```\n- On macOS and Linux:\n    ```bash\n    source venv/bin/activate\n    ```\n\n### Step 4: Install Dependencies\nInstall the required Python packages by running:\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n## How to Use Lice\nOnce the environment is set up and dependencies are installed, you can use the Lice tool to generate license files:\n\n### Step 1: Run the License Generator\nTo generate a license file, run the following command in your terminal:\n```bash\npython main.py --license <license_type> --output <output_path>\n```\nReplace `<license_type>` with the desired license (e.g., MIT, GPL) and `<output_path>` with the path where you want to save the license file.\n\n### Step 2: Verify the License File\nAfter running the command, check the specified output path for the generated license file. Ensure that the content is correct and meets your project's licensing requirements.\n\n## Conclusion\nThe Lice project is a valuable tool for developers looking to streamline their software licensing process. By following this user manual, you should be able to set up the environment and generate license files efficiently. If you have any questions or need further assistance, please refer to the documentation or contact support.", 'encoding': 'utf-8', 'mode': 'overwrite'}, 'stage': 'before'} 
